speechtext:
1.	Yes.
2.	Mr. W. R. Dawson, 3940 Cote des Neiges Road, Montreal, P.Q.
3.	Mr. Dawson is a chartered accountant. He was fully qualified to report on the following terms of reference:
(1)	A critical examination of the financial statistics furnished by the beet sugar companies;
(2)	A detailed study of their costs with comparative costs running back to 1942;
(3)	An attempt to project their costs and operating results against the possibility of operations, in the case of the Ontario and Manitoba companies, at approximately the rated capacity of the factories (this was not necessary for the Alberta company who were already operating above rated capacity) ;
(4)	An accurate study of the proportion of the value of the crop, including molasses and beet pulp, which accrued to the factories as compared to the growers;
and to obtain information:
(5)	Regarding the average return to growers on an acreage basis;
(6)	How the net return compares with competing crops.
4.	Practising chartered accountant prior to coming to Canada, in April, 1939, when he became assistant to the controller and vicepresident of the B.C. Power Corporation Limited; was engaged by the sugar administration on September 8, 1942, as director of glucose and allied products; resigned June 27, 1943, to go to South Africa in connection with personal business. On his return he was engaged, October 1, 1945, as a senior officer of the prices division of the wartime prices and trade board from which he resigned on March 31, 1946. He has had 25 years experience as a chartered accountant.
5 and 6. No.
